  "reason": "With no completed experiments, there is no evidence to favor any RNA/image encoder, profile setting, aggregation, or fusion strategy. The most informative first experiment is the simplest baseline: RNA-only, single profile, PCA n2000. It establishes a reference validation accuracy/F1 and provides a fixed anchor for later isolating the effects of multiprofile/aggregation, RNA representation, and image/multimodal fusion. Under a limited budget, this low-complexity, low-confounding baseline reduces uncertainty more efficiently than starting with a complex multimodal or multiprofile configuration."
